[primary] Abstract Classes
## Implementing Abstract Methods
- When a class is derived from an abstract superclass, the subclass inherits all of the superclass’s features, including all abstract methods.
- To replace an inherited abstract method with a concrete version, the subclass must override it.
- Abstract classes cannot be instantiated.

---

[primary] Overloading
## Overloading
- A class can have some methods which have the same name but their parameter types are different.
- Overloading addresses variations in a function's signature.
- Overloading allows binding of function calls with the same identifier but different argument types.
- The compiler binds the function call to the matching function definition.

