## Overriding
- A subclass provides the specific implementation of the method that has been declared by one of its parent classes.
- Subclasses of a class can define their own unique behaviors and yet share some of the same functionality of the parent class.

### Example: Overriding Methods
public class Rectangle {
int length;
int width;

@Override
public String toString() {
return length + "@" + width;
}
}

public class Box extends Rectangle {
int height;

return super.toString() + "@" + height;
}
}
```

## Overriding Inherited Methods
- Overridden method: An inherited method is re-written.
- Overloaded methods: Methods have the same name but their parameters are different in a class.

