Round-robin (RR) is one of the simplest
scheduling algorithms
for
processes
in an
operating system
, which assigns
time slices
to each process in equal portions and in circular order, handling all processes without
priority
. Round-robin scheduling is both simple and easy to implement, and
starvation
-free. Round-robin scheduling can also be applied to other scheduling problems, such as data packet scheduling in computer networks.
