5.1. Advantages
Improving software development efficiency involves three key elements of OOP:
Modularity: Separating tasks in the software development process based on specific objects, or each object having its own task.
Extensibility: Objects can be extended to include new attributes and behaviors in the future.

---

[optional] Reusability
Reusability: Objects can be reused within a single application or across multiple applications. Thanks to these factors, OOP helps increase software development efficiency compared to traditional procedural programming.
Improved software maintainability: Thanks to the factors mentioned above, maintenance becomes easier. Because of the modular design, changing one part of the program may not affect the rest, which is very suitable for large projects that require frequent maintenance and changes.
Faster software development: Thanks to reusability, software is developed faster. OOP often has rich object libraries, or custom-defined objects, and optimized code can all be reused in the future. => Reduced development costs.

