}
//...
}
}
2. Components of OOP
A class is an abstraction of an object. It is a template for a collection of objects that share the same attributes and methods. The structure of a class includes:
Access modifier: the scope of access to a class, property, or method. (e.g., private, protected, default, public)
Class name: Each class has a unique name to distinguish it from other classes within the same scope.
<access modifier> class <ClassName>{}
Attributes: Describe the fields used to store data for each object defined by the class, or to store references to objects of other classes. Example 2: We have two object classes A and B. Now we want to reference an object x from class B within class A, for example. This is what is written in class A.
public class A{
// Các trường lưu dữ liệu cho mỗi đối tượng:
private int y, z;
// Tham chiếu đến đối tượng x từ lớp B
private B x;
}
Methods: Each method of a class is essentially a function written specifically for the objects of that class, and is called to interact with those objects. Example 3:
// Lớp Err
public class Err{
// Các thuộc tính
private String title;
private String mess;
// Phương thức
public void inputData(String tt, String m){
title = tt;
mess = m;
}
public void output(){
System.out.println("Err " + title + ": " + mess);
}
}
// Hàm main
public static void main(String args[]){
// Khai báo, khởi tạo đối tượng
Err x = new Err();
// Tác động vào đối tượng
x.input("Error 2001", "- Lỗi này tạm thời chưa có nội dung");
x.output();
}

