### Exception Propagations

```text
catch(...)
A()
B()
Stack for A()
Stack for B()
C()
Stack for C()
D()
Exception
Stack for D()
```

Stack trace:
- When an exception occurs at a method, the program stack contains running methods (e.g., method A calls method B, etc.).
- This allows tracing statements related to the exception.

[Image Summary: PDF Page 13 Image 1]
public class ExceptionPropagate {
public void mA() {
mB();
}
public void mB() {
mC();
}
public void mC() {
System.out.println(5 / 0);
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
ExceptionPropagate obj = new ExceptionPropagate();
obj.mA();
}
}
Output:
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.ArithmeticException: / by zero
at ExceptionPropagate.mC(ExceptionPropagate.java:12)
at ExceptionPropagate.mB(ExceptionPropagate.java:8)
at ExceptionPropagate.mA(ExceptionPropagate.java:4)
at ExceptionPropagate.main(ExceptionPropagate.java:16)

